[?25l[0m[38;5;141m> [0m[38;5;252m[1m## What was wrong and what I changed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
There were two bugs in the C-to-Rust translation:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 1: Missing [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m symbol export[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The test runner dynamically loads the compiled [38;5;10mlibblake.so[0m and looks up the symbol [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m (the C code uses [38;5;10m#define hash_message SPX_NAMESPACE(hash_message)[0m which expands to [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m). The Rust [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m only exported [38;5;10mcrypto_sign_*[0m functions — it never exposed [38;5;10mSPX_hash_message[0m as an [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m function.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m:[22m Added an [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern "C" fn SPX_hash_message(...)[0m wrapper that converts raw pointers to Rust slices/references and delegates to [38;5;10mhash::hash_message()[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m### Bug 2: Incorrect [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m datalen parameter (bits vs bytes mismatch)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m function takes [38;5;10mdatalen[0m in [1mbits[22m (internally it does [38;5;10mdatalen >> 3[0m to get bytes). The C [38;5;10mhash_blake.c[0m passes raw byte counts like [38;5;10mSPX_N[0m (16) directly — meaning it actually hashes only 2 bytes (16 bits) per call, not 16 bytes. This is arguably a quirk of the C code, but it's the behavior the test vectors are generated from.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The Rust translation "corrected" this by multiplying by 8 ([38;5;10m(SPX_N as u64) * 8[0m), which would hash 16 bytes (128 bits) — producing different output than the C code.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mFix in [38;5;10mhash.rs[0m:[22m Removed the [38;5;10m* 8[0m multiplications in both [38;5;10mgen_message_random[0m and [38;5;10mhash_message[0m, passing byte counts directly to [38;5;10mblake256_update[0m to match the C behavior exactly:[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m(SPX_N as u64) * 8[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_N as u64[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10m(SPX_PK_BYTES as u64) * 8[0m → [38;5;10mSPX_PK_BYTES as u64[0m[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mmlen * 8[0m → [38;5;10mmlen[0m[0m[0m
